  "id": "simsimiyya_suez_canal",
  "name": "Simsimiyya (Suez Canal lyre song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song of the Canal Zone cities of Port Said, Ismailia and Suez, accompanied by the simsimiyya lyre at weddings and neighbourhood gatherings, where a lead singer and a male chorus trade verses of love, the sea and the Canal cities' wartime resistance. The El Tanbura band, founded in Port Said at the end of the 1980s by Zakaria Ibrahim, revived the older Port Said repertoire and recorded it for international labels.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1980s simsimiyya, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. single lead single track no stacking. five string metal strung strum and damp call-and-response simsimiyya, riq, Egyptian sombaty canonical mid east darbuka, hand clap. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
